& [Conflict] is representational not semantic absence
  + a finite JSON Schema document may describe an infinite recursively shaped instance language using a local reference cycle
  + finite document bytes do not make every instance finite-resource safe
  + finite unrolling would change accepted public shape or create an arbitrary duplicate depth ceiling
  + separate transport projection would introduce translation and drift without removing the semantic recursion already present

& [Delineation] is three boundaries
  + schema graph finiteness governs generator termination and canonical bytes
  + JSON container depth governs parser and validator resource safety
  + ProcedureType and ProcedureValue depth governs Cantor semantic validity
  - never: represent one boundary as proof of another

